course: dictionary
lesson: 6016
title: Medicine: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word medicine has three meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. It can be a pill, liquid or cream that helps you get better when ill. It can be the science and work of doctors. It can also be anything that makes you feel better, as in «Laughter is the best medicine».
explain: Look at the words around it. «Before a new medicine is sold, it is tested on many volunteers» means a pill or liquid, because it is tested and sold. «Studying medicine» means the science, because you study a subject, not a pill.
explain: Medicine is never candy, even if it tastes sweet. Only take medicine from a trusted adult, in the right dose, and always read the label first.
fact: «Medicine» means a pill, liquid or cream that helps you get better when you are ill.
fact: Medicine can also mean the science and work of doctors, as in «studying medicine».
fact: Taking more of a medicine than the dose on the label can poison you, even with common medicines like paracetamol.
fact: If you swallow medicine by mistake, tell an adult at once, and call a poison helpline if one is needed.
fact: Keep medicine locked away from small children, and never take someone else's medicine.
exercise: «Medicine is not candy.» What does this tell you? | *Medicine must be treated with care, even if it tastes sweet | Medicine is only for pets | Medicine can be eaten like sweets | Medicine is always sour
exercise: «He wants to study medicine at university.» What does medicine mean here? | Something that makes you laugh | A cream for sore skin | *The science and work of doctors | A pill to stop a cough
exercise: Your nan says a new medicine is safe. What should you check first? | Its price | Its colour | *The label and the dose | Its smell
test: «Taking more of a medicine than the dose on the label can poison you.» What does dose mean here? | The shop where you buy it | *The amount you should take | The box it comes in | The name of the medicine
test: Anna finds her brother's medicine on the bathroom floor. What should she do first? | *Tell a trusted adult at once | Eat one, in case it is sweet | Hide it in her pocket | Put it in her school bag
exam: Why is it dangerous to take someone else's medicine? | It only works on Tuesdays | It always tastes bad | *It may not be right for you or the right dose | It makes you taller
